---
title: "Figure 7 — Operator Console: login, session, and role-based approval flow"
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Operator / Viewer
    participant B as Browser
    participant C as Console (Flask)
    participant US as UserStore<br/>(werkzeug hashes)
    participant Q as ApprovalQueue<br/>(shared with monitor)

    Note over U,C: 1 — Authentication
    U->>B: open console
    B->>C: GET /login
    C-->>B: login form
    U->>B: username + password
    B->>C: POST /login
    C->>US: verify(username, password)
    alt invalid
        US-->>C: None
        C-->>B: 401 — re-render with error
    else valid
        US-->>C: User(role)
        C->>C: session.clear(); new CSRF token; login_at = seen_at = now
        C-->>B: 302 → signed cookie {user, role, login_at, seen_at, csrf}<br/>(HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax)
    end

    Note over U,C: 2 — Every subsequent request
    B->>C: GET /dashboard | /approvals | /policy | /sequence | /audit
    C->>C: login_required — signed in and not expired?
    Note right of C: expired = idle > 30 min<br/>or > 8 h since login;<br/>a valid request refreshes the idle timer
    alt no session, or expired
        C-->>B: 302 → /login (expired session cleared)
    else authenticated
        C-->>B: 200 — rendered view (read-only observation)
    end

    Note over U,Q: 3 — Acting on a gate (role- and CSRF-gated)
    B->>C: POST /approvals/{id}/approve + csrf_token
    C->>C: requires_role(operator) + CSRF check
    alt viewer, or CSRF token missing / invalid
        C-->>B: 403
    else operator + valid token
        C->>Q: resolve(approval_id, approved, operator)
        Q-->>C: PendingApproval(status)
        Note right of Q: unblocks the monitor's wait;<br/>the monitor writes<br/>ApprovalResolutionEvent<br/>(operator as SHA-256 digest)
        C-->>B: 302 → /approvals (flash result)
    end

    Note over U,C: 4 — Logout (POST + CSRF)
    B->>C: POST /logout + csrf_token
    alt valid token
        C-->>B: 302 → /login (session cleared)
    else token missing / invalid
        C-->>B: 302 → /login (session left intact)
    end
